Queensland private schools have stayed at the top of the academic peak rankings, and this will continue in 2018 with outstanding exam results, reinforced by personal and shared success in sport, the arts, the music and other community ventures.
These schools with a total of more than 30,000 pupils enrogating across Scotland, represented by the Scottish Private School Council (SCIS), are trying to provide the best service for their pupils and their parents.
The aim of private schools is to prepare pupils for additional and higher education, for their chosen professions and their place as world citizens.
As an education sector capable of designing and implementing a curriculum tailored to circumstances, we can see that modern languages continue to be well-recognised in schools and the subjects they want.
Nelson Mandela said: "When you talk to a person in the language that understands him, it gets to his mind.
